/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  curate23_vp_diethylethanolamine -- the vapour pressure of diethylethanolamine, REFITTED to
  measurements (DEV.md 4c C281 step 2).  Written by `bin/choupo-curate vp
  diethylethanolamine`; everything above the RESULT paragraph is the DECLARATION, committed
  before any fit ran, so it can be read against the result.

  WHY.  The catalogue record carried `vaporPressure { model AmbroseWalton; }`,
  a corresponding-states ESTIMATE from Tc, Pc and omega that never reads the
  record's own Tb (C279 measured a median 19.6 % AAD over the 25 such records
  with archive data).  Here a three-parameter Antoine is fitted to ONE
  laboratory and held out on ANOTHER that shares no author with it.

  STUDIES (one per article, extracted by `choupo-thermoml extract-vp`; ranked
  by points, ties by DOI):
      10.1021/je049761y                31 pts  278.2-318.3 K  Kapteina; Slovik; Verevkin; Heintz
      10.1016/j.fluid.2018.05.032      24 pts  273.64-308.15 K  Soares; Stejfa; Ferreira; Pinho et al.
      10.1021/je101259r                13 pts  333.2-449.5 K  Klepacova; Huttenhuis; Derks; Versteeg
  SET ASIDE BY NAME:
      10.1021/je301219c: 2 pressure point(s), fewer than 5
      10.1021/je4008712: 2 pressure point(s), fewer than 5

  PARTITION (the C16 rule, declared): FIT = the study with the most points,
  doi 10.1021/je049761y (31 pts, 278.2-318.3 K); HELD OUT =
  the next largest sharing no author with it, doi 10.1016/j.fluid.2018.05.032 (24 pts,
  273.64-308.15 K).

  BAND: maxAAD 1.7 % (declared before the fit by bin/choupo-curate vp (C281 step 2): the held-out study's own stated relative expanded uncertainty U95(P)/P, AVERAGED over its 24 points (1.06 to 2.47 %, mean 1.664 %), rounded UP to two significant figures -- a mean held against the held-out AAD, which is a mean).

  NORMAL BOILING POINT: the record's Tb 434.15 K lies OUTSIDE the measured span 273.64-318.3 K: the fitted Antoine's own normal boiling point (P = 101.325 kPa) must lie within 2 K of it, or the fit is NOT promoted (an extrapolation that misses the record's own boiling point).

  NO MEASURED POINT IS IN THIS TREE: constant/archiveDatasets declares both
  series by DOI, NIST URL and sha256; `bin/choupo-curate fetch` regenerates
  them into constant/archiveExtracts/ (gitignored).

  RESULT
  @@RESULT-BEGIN@@
  WHAT THE RUN FOUND (pinned in `expected`; measured, not argued).
  Antoine log10(Psat/bar) = 5.211269 - 1996.8790/(T + -43.7040),
  in-sample R2 0.999590 over 31 points, 278.2-318.3 K. HELD OUT: 24
  points, AAD 3.5664 % against the band 1.7 % -> notValidated. Its own
  normal boiling point (101.325 kPa): 427.31 K. NOT PROMOTED: held-out
  verdict notValidated (AAD 3.566 % against the band 1.7 % declared
  before the fit); the record keeps AmbroseWalton
  @@RESULT-END@@
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

operations
(
    {
        name       fit_antoine;
        type       vaporPressureFit;
        component  diethylethanolamine;

        evidence
        (
            {
                dataset   "constant/archiveExtracts/diethylethanolamine-vapourPressure-je049761y.dat";
                identity  { doi "10.1021/je049761y"; }
                role      fit;
            }
            {
                dataset   "constant/archiveExtracts/diethylethanolamine-vapourPressure-j.fluid.2018.05.032.dat";
                identity  { doi "10.1016/j.fluid.2018.05.032"; }
                role      validation;
            }
        );

        acceptance
        {
            maxAAD  1.7 percent;
            origin  "declared before the fit by bin/choupo-curate vp (C281 step 2): the held-out study's own stated relative expanded uncertainty U95(P)/P, AVERAGED over its 24 points (1.06 to 2.47 %, mean 1.664 %), rounded UP to two significant figures -- a mean held against the held-out AAD, which is a mean";
        }

        output     { file fit_antoine.csv; }
    }
);
